Thanks for all your advice!

I wished for a ring of free action, [GoD, a spellbook of FoD (for
emergencies), and an amulet of life saving. After a magic marker
session and finally finding fort Ludios, I got my AC to -33. A friendly
nurse gave me a good +30 max HP which was nice.

I've just beaten Master Kaen, but man oh man it was a war of attrition.
I kept getting him down to 30HP and having to duck out because I was at
30HP too. I tried floating above the lava and emptying all of my wands
into him; this seemed to be what won it. However, I'd taken off my
shield and donned my robe for spellcasting, making me MR and
reflection-less; one of his lightning bolts destroyed my rings of
levitation and free action. Also at one point he killed me, making me
very glad I wished for that amulet.

I came to be thankful for the insects he kept summoning - they were a
good living wall. I came to be irritated by the fact that you can't
teleport to lava, so every now and then I'd be flushed from my
hiding-place by my own teleportitis.

When he died, it was completely unexpected since I hadn't done much
damage to him for some time. I had emptied a few wands into him, and he
had stuck on the upstairs for quite a while. Then suddenly he
teleported to me (at this point he destroyed my rings) and next hit I
killed him. Maybe his own insects beat him up - I had conflict at the
time.

I can see now why he has such a fearsome rep. (It *really* doesn't help
that monks have a hard time dealing significant damage.)

Still got 2 wishes left. Don't think I'll replace the ring or amulet. I
think that the WoY will be a piece of cake compared to the old Master.
I might wish for an AoR, so I can take the shield off without losing
reflection. Or maybe a +2 ring of increase damage.

In the meantime, my god has given me Werebane and Dragonbane. I'm
almost tempted to use Werebane... after all, it *is* silver..

